  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 AM EST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nShortwave trof is moving east away from MI. Just some cirrus with it \nearlier, not enough forcing to do more given our paucity of \nmoisture. Though the most significant thermal boundary will remain \nstrung out just to our north, an initial cool front has passed, \ntemporarily halting warm advection. Some post-frontal lower cloud \ncover has expanded into parts of eastern upper MI. Surface high \npressure over WV and environs is extending a ridge axis nw-ward into \nthe western lakes. This ridge crosses northern MI early this \nmorning, and we return to warm advection and southerly flow by this \nafternoon.\n\nQuiet and mild wx continues into the start of the weekend. Mostly \ncloudy skies will expand across the eastern UP early this morning, \nbut will be advected ne-ward back out of the area this afternoon. \nThat will be partially replaced by warm advection cirrus pushing \neast into northern MI today. Nw lower MI will be about as warm today \nas yesterday, the rest of the area will be a few degrees cooler. \nQuiet tonight, though increasing mid/high clouds, especially central \nand north. Those clouds diminish Saturday morning, and period of \nmostly sunny skies is expected Saturday everywhere but the eastern \nUP. Somewhat cloudier in the UP, and maybe just maybe a stray shower \ncan reach western Chip Co late in the day. Saturday still looks like \nthe warmest day of this warm spell, and record highs will be \nthreatened at multiple sites (in order of likelihood, PLN/GLR/HTL/ \nAPN/ANJ/TVC). Breezy s to sw winds.\n\nTroffing will become more established in the n central states late \nthis weekend. An initial southern stream wave weakens quickly Sat \nnight, but a pair of more vigorous northern stream waves late Sunday \nand late Monday will drastically lower heights here. Surface low \npressure passing well to our north will tend to weaken, but \neventually a stronger cold front crosses northern MI Sunday. That is \nalso when our best chance for showers finally arrives, and a period \nof rain (and just rain) is expected in most of northern MI. A chance \nof nw flow lake effect precip Sun night into Monday night, with an \ninitial mix turning to just snow. Plenty of instability, but we are \nquickly drying out, so just chancy pops for now. Then high pressure \ncrosses the area, so drying out Tue-Wed. Highs in the 30s to near \n40f next week.",
